### [AG] AGRICULTURE, RURAL DEVELOPMENT, FOOD AND DRUG ADMINISTRATION, AND RELATED AGENCIES
$6,957,972,000 [[num:src_ag_cee4dfd9_de7e_40f0_b82e_f896328a8490_1]] is appropriated for FDA Salaries and Expenses in FY2026.

Major allowed uses include:
- necessary expenses of the Food and Drug Administration, including hire and purchase of passenger motor vehicles and space rental/special-purpose space;
- enforcement-related and emergency expenses, including miscellaneous enforcement expenses up to $25,000;
- Human Foods Program and related field activities;
- drug, biologics, device, veterinary, and tobacco product programs and related field activities;
- the National Center for Toxicological Research;
- rent and related activities, including payments to GSA and White Oak consolidation;
- other FDA activities, including the Office of the Commissioner, the Office of the Chief Scientist, the Office of the Chief Medical Officer, and central services.

User fees are also credited to the account and remain available until expended.

