### [AG] AGRICULTURE, RURAL DEVELOPMENT, FOOD AND DRUG ADMINISTRATION, AND RELATED AGENCIES

The USDA Food Safety and Inspection Service receives $1,215,200,000 [[num:src_ag_edc59832_2cb3_4b5e_8135_dc08af3b46e9_1]] for necessary expenses to carry out services authorized by the Federal Meat Inspection Act, the Poultry Products Inspection Act, and the Egg Products Inspection Act, including up to $10,000 for representation allowances and expenses under section 8 of the 1956 Act. In addition, $1,000,000 [[num:src_ag_edc59832_2cb3_4b5e_8135_dc08af3b46e9_2]] may be credited to the account from laboratory accreditation fees.

Major funded activities include:
- meat, poultry, and egg inspection services;
- the Public Health Data Communication Infrastructure system;
- inspections and enforcement related to the Humane Methods of Slaughter Act, with no fewer than 148 full-time equivalent positions dedicated to those duties.

